---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import WebhookGenerator from '../../components/WebhookGenerator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Webhook Payload Generator"
  description="Generate sample webhook JSON payloads (Stripe, GitHub, Slack-style) for testing your webhook handler locally — no live account needed."
>
  <WebhookGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why test with sample payloads</h2>
  <p>
    Testing a webhook handler often means waiting for a real event to fire —
    slow and inconvenient during development. Having a realistic sample
    payload lets you test your parsing and business logic immediately,
    without triggering a real transaction or push.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Pick the payload shape closest to what you're building against.</li>
    <li>Copy the JSON and use it in your local testing (e.g. curl, Postman, or a unit test fixture).</li>
    <li>Click Regenerate for a fresh sample with new random IDs.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Webhook Payload FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Are these official payload formats?</strong> No — they're
    illustrative samples modeled after common webhook shapes. Always verify
    exact field names against the real provider's official documentation
    before deploying.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
